            <ArticleTitle>Propofol-induced bronchoconstriction: two case reports.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>645-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Bronchoconstriction was induced by anesthetic induction with propofol in two patients with allergic diseases. One had severe bronchospasm improved by epinephrine. Propofol should be used with caution in patients with allergic disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
